    {
      "name": "hunting_onset",
      "description": "Reference vector 2 (oscillating: short-window scatter 2.5 against a long-window 0.4). SAT is flat at 13 °C for 2.5 h — long enough for madLong to converge on ~0 across a full 2 h baseline — then a ±3 °C 15-min square wave starts at t=9000 s. madShort clears 1.2 at t=9450 s and both conditions hold; persist asserts 1800 s later at t=11250 s. The alarm then self-clears at t=12600 s: by then half the 2 h baseline window is itself oscillating, madLong has risen past madShort/2, and the ratio test releases. Asserted windows keep two 150 s steps of margin from both edges.",
